# PROJECT.md — copy this to the root of the repo you work in

`dev-workflow` deliberately hardcodes nothing about your branches, board or hosts. Copy this file to
`PROJECT.md` (or `.claude/PROJECT.md`) in your own repository and fill it in. The skills read the values
from here; where one is missing they will ask rather than guess.

## Branches

| Placeholder | Your value | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `FEATURE_BRANCH` | | Where day-to-day work lands, e.g. `alice-dev` |
| `MR_TARGET_BRANCH` | | What MRs target, e.g. `develop` or `milestone-aug-2026` |
| `INTEGRATION_BRANCH` | | First branch after merge, if you have one |
| `STAGING_BRANCH` | | What staging deploys from |
| `PREPROD_BRANCH` | | Pre-production sign-off branch, if you have one |
| `PROD_BRANCH` | | What production deploys from |

**Promotion:** does each step run through CI/CD, or does someone pull manually? Say which — it changes
what may be assumed to have happened after a merge.

## Git host

| Placeholder | Your value |
|---|---|
| `GITLAB_HOST` | e.g. `https://gitlab.com` or a self-hosted URL |
| `GITLAB_PROJECT_ID` | numeric project id, only needed for API calls that require it |

Token: export `GITLAB_TOKEN`, or let it resolve from your git credential helper. **Never** put a token
in this file, and never commit one.

## Ticket tracker

| Placeholder | Your value |
|---|---|
| `JIRA_HOST` | e.g. `https://yourcompany.atlassian.net` |
| Ticket key prefix | e.g. `PROJ` — used in commit messages as `[PROJ-1234]` |

Fill in the transition ids once, from the API — they are per-workflow and change when the board is
edited:

```bash
curl -s -u "$JIRA_EMAIL:$JIRA_TOKEN" \
  "$JIRA_HOST/rest/api/3/issue/<TICKET-KEY>/transitions" | jq '.transitions[]|{id,name}'
```

| Status | Transition id |
|---|---|
| In Progress | |
| Code Review | |
| Deployed to staging | |
| Staging verified | |
| On production | |
| Production verified | |

## Paths

| Env var | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `TASK_DOCS_DIR` | `$HOME/task-notes` | Where per-task notes and review docs are written |
| `VIDEO_DIR` | `$TASK_DOCS_DIR/videos` | Where verification recordings land |
| `REVIEWER_SLUG` | `$(whoami)` | Used in self-review filenames |

## Stack

Say what the project is (framework, language, test runner, linter). The skills use it to pick the right
lint command and the right patterns to check in review — otherwise they guess from the file extensions.
